<h2>Why people came</h2>

<p>ONS publishes a breakdown by reason for <strong>non-EU+ arrivals only</strong>, which were
{% figure "migration/non-eu-plus-long-term-immigration" %} of the {% figure "migration/total-long-term-immigration" %} total. Non-EU+ is a
nationality grouping, not a route. There is no headline breakdown of net migration by reason:
subtracting this year's departures, classified by the reason they originally came, from this
year's arrivals would set two different cohorts against each other.</p>

